Here's how to handle each scenario in MSTest:

## 1. Windows-only tests

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
// Or use the built-in platform check:
[TestMethod]
public void RegistryTest()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows");
    // ... registry code
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGPU")]
public void GpuTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI - requires local GPU");
    // ... GPU code
}
```

Then exclude in CI with: `dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=RequiresGPU"`

## 3. Flaky external API — use retry

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // MSTest 3.x+ built-in retry attribute
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    var result = CallWeatherApi();
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

For older MSTest versions without `[Retry]`, wrap the call manually:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    Exception last = null;
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        try { CallWeatherApi(); return; }
        catch (Exception ex) { last = ex; Thread.Sleep(1000); }
    }
    Assert.Fail($"Failed after 3 retries: {last!.Message}");
}
```

## 4. Cleanup even on failure — use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string _tempFile = null!;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs even if the test fails
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFileTest()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile, "data");
        // ... test logic that might throw
    }
}
```

`[TestCleanup]` is the idiomatic MSTest approach — it always runs after each test method regardless of pass/fail, similar to `finally`.

**Summary:**

| Scenario | Pattern |
|----------|---------|
| OS-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` / platform guard |
| Skip in CI | `[TestCategory]` + filter, or env-var check |
| Flaky API | `[Retry(3)]` (MSTest 3.x+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` method |
